⚖️ **F-1680-1 (s1680 2026-08-11, MEASURED ON THE TWELFTH CONSECUTIVE HELD FIRE — A "SAME IN BOTH ARMS" RESULT RETIRES A *COMPARATOR*, AND F-1677-1'S LEAF-FLIP GUARD WAS NEVER A COMPARATOR. IT WAS RETIRED ANYWAY, ACROSS TWO FIRES, AND THE OPERATIVE INSTRUCTION NOW SAYS THE OPPOSITE OF THE FINDING IT CITES AS STANDING. NOT AN OWNER QUESTION; DOES NOT JOIN THE DESK.)** 📋 **BOARD, MEASURED NOT COPIED:** `find tasks/queue -type f` → **0** · no `tasks/CODEX-WALL` · assayer `pending/` EMPTY · every `tasks/done/` head entry `drained-`/`stopped-` · lanes b/c/d USABLE-but-behind (93/282/133) · lane-a **BUSY** throughout. **Nothing to drain, nothing lawful to author, dispatch held.** 🩺 **LIVENESS, SELF-COLLECTED VIA THE INVARIANT PHRASE (F-1676-1):** `grep "Serial progress"` → **835 → 906 / 1,706; 161 failures observed** (**ADVANCING**, monotonic); log mtime **23:11** read at **23:13** (**ALIVE**). ✅ **THE HOLD SURVIVES ITS OWN AUDIT AND I READ ITS GROUNDS AT SOURCE RATHER THAN COUNTING THE CITATIONS.** F-1670-1's text names two, and both hold today: f1643-2's own gate (*"only when all four lanes are idle and no drain is in flight… state the concurrent load it ran under"*) and **the owner's THROTTLE LAW** (*"I woke up in the middle of the night to it."*). Dispatching `f1662-2` into a live `--workers=3` + `nice -n 19` run would add exactly the concurrent load the first forbids recording and the second forbids creating. **Confirmed, not overturned.** 🎯 **THE FINDING — THE GUARD WAS MEASURED ON THE WRONG AXIS AND RETIRED ON THE RESULT.** **s1677** established a leaf-flip condition in as many words: *"BEFORE THE LEAF FLIP, APPLY F-1677-1: `grep -c "Not classified"` on the merged copy — **non-zero ⇒ leave the leaf `queued`**; only a section carrying real rows earns the `queued`→`merged` flip."* **s1678** then ran that grep against **both** arms, got **1 and 1**, and correctly concluded the salvage *introduces* nothing — its finding text is explicit that *"S1677'S ACTION CALL WAS SO