🧪 **F-1679-1 (s1679 2026-08-11, MEASURED ON THE ELEVENTH CONSECUTIVE HELD FIRE — I RAN A SECOND PROBE TO CONFIRM A FIRST, AND IT CONFIRMED IT. BOTH WERE WRONG, FOR TWO UNRELATED MECHANICAL REASONS, AND THE DISCONFIRMING CONTROL WAS ALREADY PRINTED ON MY OWN SCREEN. NOT AN OWNER QUESTION.)** 📋 **THE NEAR-MISS, stated first because the finding is about how close it came:** while pre-proving the banked `f1662-2` dispatch I asked whether its Step 1 refresh target exists, ran `git rev-parse --short main origin/main`, and got **rc=128 `fatal: Needed a single revision`** with **no output at all**. Read while asking *does this ref exist?*, that text says **no**. 🔁 **I THEN DID THE RIGHT-LOOKING THING AND CHECKED IT A SECOND WAY** — `git for-each-ref --format='%(refname) %(objectname:short)' refs/remotes/origin/ | grep -E "origin/(main|master|HEAD)$"` → **0 hits**. Two independent commands, same answer. The finding I was one commit from filing: *"`origin/main` does not exist, so `f1662-2`'s Step 1 refresh target is missing and the dispatch would fail"* — dramatic, actionable, and **completely false**; it would have frozen a ready dispatch behind a phantom infrastructure defect. ✓ **BOTH MECHANISMS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED.** (1) **`--short` TAKES ONE REVISION.** `git rev-parse main origin/main` (same two revs, no `--short`) prints **both** hashes fine: `d19a5c1fd30b…` and `f8a6af221d16…`. The message is about the **ARITY OF MY ARGUMENT LIST**, not about any revision failing to resolve — an error text that **accuses the wrong subject**, the same shape as the false *"lane is stale"* STOP that F-1424-3/F-1668-1 were filed for. (2) **`$` CANNOT ANCHOR AGAINST A MULTI-FIELD `--format`.** Each line read `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD f8a6af221`, so the anchor sat before a space, not at end-of-line. Same pattern, one-field format: `git for-each-ref --format='%(refname)' … | grep -cE "origin/(main|master|HEAD)$"` → **2**; two-field → **0**. **The `--format` field count silently decides whet