g rather than move into the pre-merge battery"), so it contradicts nothing: the guard **SKIPs on an `ACTIVE` lock line**, so it is a no-op mid-fire and bites only after the handoff commit, which is when the desk exists. ✅ `gate-caller-audit` re-run after the change: **PASS** (reachability is computed from ROOTS and `test:ledger-guards` is deliberately unrooted, so the grandfather entry stays correct and stays needed). 🩹 **THE INHERITED DESK IS REPAIRED IN THIS FIRE'S OWN HANDOFF, not merely reported:** all **21** items are carried forward with **one 🔺 each**, restoring the format the parser reads. The true set is not my reconstruction — it is `desk-state-audit --status` run against **s1664's** archived line-1, which returns `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=0 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=21 · UNRECORDED=0`, i.e. **nothing among the 21 has silently closed and none is a ghost.** ⓘ **No new mechanism is proposed for the `·`-run encoding itself** — the count refusal already catches it (`declared 21` vs `keyed 1`), and it went unseen only because the guard holding that check was never run. **Wiring the existing guard is the whole cure.**
