🧹 **F-1665-1 (s1665 2026-08-11, MEASURED ON A DRY BOARD — A THIRD OF `scripts/` IS SINGLE-FIRE SCRATCH, IT IS DEGRADING A LANE INSTRUMENT, AND THE OBVIOUS CURE MAKES THE SYMPTOM 25× WORSE. NOT AN OWNER QUESTION.)** 📋 **THE MEASUREMENT:** `git ls-files scripts/` → **421 tracked files, 151 of them (35.9%) `tmp-*` single-fire scratch, minted by 38 distinct fires** from s1045 to s1664 — the lock/handoff/ledger/desk helpers a fire writes to splice `STATUS.md` and `goals.json` under the backtick-prose law, then commits. ⚠️ **WHY IT IS NOT COSMETIC: `scripts` is one of the nine entries in `lane-usable.mjs`'s `RUN_SURFACE`**, whose design comment (F-1343-2) calls the list *"deliberately narrow: only surfaces that can change whether a task runs or how it is gated"* and excludes `docs/ tasks/ artifacts/ reviews/ logs/` **BY DESIGN** — its whole worth is that a small number is readable where a large one is not. 📊 **Measured on the live fleet: `lane/b`'s run-surface drift reads 5 files, ALL FIVE s1664 lock/handoff scratch — a 100% false signal.** That flips the tool out of its `drift.length === 0` branch (`lane-usable.mjs:384`), so instead of the ✅ *"NONE of it is run-surface … nothing here can stop a task running"* green, the most refillable lane on a dry board shows an amber telling the next fire to go prove `merge-base --is-ancestor` for dead files. Lanes a/c/d read **18 / 74 / 34** where only **13 / 60 / 20** are real. ✗ **ONE HYPOTHESIS REFUTED BEFORE IT WAS ACTED ON, recorded because the next reader will have it too:** I expected the scratch to DISPLACE real entries past the 8-line display cutoff (`:403`). **It does not** — `tmp-*` sorts alphabetically last, so `real files invisible today` equals `invisible if scratch were gone` on every lane (5/52/12, identical both ways). The harm is the false amber and the inflated count, nothing more. ⛔ **AND THE OBVIOUS CURE — SWEEP `scripts/tmp-*` — IS REFUTED ON THREE INDEPENDENT GROUNDS. DO NOT DO IT.** **(1) IT INVERTS ITS OWN ME