rted lines, which is the tell. I had inferred the `—`-escaping convention from the *titles* — written by an older serializer — and generalised it to a file that no longer obeys it. **Narrowed the denominator to the text I generate**, which is the only thing a splice can be responsible for. Same family as the guard-denominator findings: a check whose subject is wider than its author's change reports other people's history as your defect. 📁 Splice script retained in-repo per the RETENTION LAW (`scripts/tmp-s1664-price-leaves.mjs`); it refuses on a missing/duplicate id, a pre-existing block, non-ASCII in its own output, and any parse or tree-shape change outside `authoringBlock`.
