is cheap to fix: the factory's ENTIRE authorable-candidate surface is TWELVE `planned` leaves** (against 666 `merged` / 57 `shipped` / 25 `superseded` / 11 `verified-by-owner` / 5 `building` / 5 `stopped` / 3 `blocked`). **Before this fire: 2 priced, 10 unpriced.** Four fires each burned an authoring budget choosing among twelve rows, none of which recorded what the last fire learned. ✅ **CURED, in the leaf and in an instrument.** (1) The three already-paid measurements are transcribed onto their leaves as a structured `authoringBlock` {class · finding · measuredBy · reason} — `ap16-6-action-verbs` ← F-1649-1, `ap-03-protocol` ← F-1650-1, `ap-15-assay-of-minds` ← F-1653-2. Spliced, never re-serialized: **21 insertions, 3 deletions** (the three `status` lines gaining a comma). (2) `scripts/authorable-candidates.mjs` lists all twelve with their class and citation in one command; **advisory, exit 0** by the `drain-block-check` UNKNOWN precedent — `--strict` is opt-in, because 7 unpriced legacy leaves would otherwise red the whole board rather than answer the question asked. (3) `scripts/authorable-candidates.test.mjs`, **10 tests, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`**, each red path proven by **manufacturing the defect** on fixtures (unpriced leaf → `--strict` rc=1; a typo'd class `owner-frok` → degraded to `unclassified` and *said so* rather than trusted; an `authoringBlock` with no `reason` → does NOT read as priced). ⚖️ **READ THE CLASS, NOT JUST THE PRICE — this is F-1383-1's discriminator moved from draining to authoring, and it is the half that decides who is owed.** Of the three: **`ap-15-assay-of-minds` is OWNER-GATED** (3 open ratification questions — it belongs on the desk, and F-1653-2 already has it there); **`ap16-6-action-verbs` and `ap-03-protocol` are ATTENDED-OWED** — no owner word will ever lift them, so carrying them to the desk would park them forever, exactly as a `gate-side` block carried as `owner-fork` does. 📉 **STATE AFTER: 5 priced (1 owner-gated ·