ited and the old gate struck through as SUPERSEDED-DO-NOT-ACT · `ap-04` and `ap-05` titles retired their stale imperatives (2-line splice, `goals.json` re-parsed OK — never re-serialized) · the archived **`AGENT PLAY pace set`** row marked SUPERSEDED, kept because two other surfaces cite it by that exact grep key. 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT MECHANISED, following F-1614-1's own restraint and its explicit instruction to measure precision FIRST:** widening the guard to `specs/**` means parsing prohibition prose out of spec heads — a judgement surface, and judgement guards earn a permanent excused red (the `cross-engine` fate, F-1460-1). **The cheap discipline that would have caught it needs no mechanism: when a ruling names its own GATE surface, OPEN THAT SURFACE IN THE SAME FIRE — the ruling tells you where to look, in words, for free.** 💡 *Reusable shape: **a ruling is not delivered when it is recorded, it is delivered when every surface that can still say NO has stopped saying it** — and the last one to be flipped is reliably the one the ruling itself nominated, because naming a gate feels like discharging it.* ⚠️ **SCOPE, STATED HONESTLY: I did NOT clear the other six longer-horizon leaves** (`rf-04-bounty`, `rf-05-fixed-version`, `map-campaign-27`, `stream-live`, `ap-15-assay-of-minds`, `foundry-first-real-game`) beyond reading their titles — all six read owner-gated on their face (owner copy/prizes · owner vE1.0 tag + walk blessing · the 0/25 OWNER TEST column, whose leaf says in as many words *"Do NOT author a wiring or landmark master"* · owner starts the loop · spec DRAFT + 3 ratification Qs · owner brings the seed). **`bt-04-homestead-automation` I checked and it is NOT authorable** — F-1614-1 already ruled it *"unblocked as a **program** but still missing its four **parameters**"*, and the parameters (what X% is, what idle means) are exactly the design forks §7.3 reserves for the owner. **GATE: none owed to the owner — this is a bookkeeping propagation of a ruling