🟢 **F-1633-1 (s1633 2026-08-10, MEASURED BY RUNNING THREE NEEDLES OVER ONE CORPUS — THE GZ-01 SWEEP DUTY WAS CARRIED AS "OWED" FOR THREE FIRES WHILE THE BOARD WAS CLEAN, BECAUSE THE LAWS PRESCRIBED 8-CHAR NEEDLE IS DERIVED WITH `%h`, WHICH ABBREVIATES TO 9 IN THIS REPO).** Non-blocking, doc-only, no code owed. 🔎 **HOW IT SURFACED:** s1631 and s1632 both handed off *"GZ-01 backfill sweep still owed"* as a priority item, so I ran it. It was not owed — s1600 discharged it, s1608 and s1610 re-ran it, and every drain since s1607 files its GZ-01 item inline at drain-bookkeeping time (visible in `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md`s own git log). **A duty that is already discharged but still recited costs every fire that inherits it a full budget to re-derive.** That is Mistake #4 wearing a standing-order costume. 🔑 **THE MECHANISM, AND IT SITS INSIDE F-1600-1s OWN CURE:** that finding correctly prescribes grepping *the 8-char short hash across the WHOLE of `marketing/outbox/`*. But a fire obtains its candidate hashes with `git log --format=%h`, and **git auto-abbreviates by object count — in this repo that is now 9 characters**. A 9-char needle cannot match an 8-char citation, so **the method is right and the needle is wrong**, reproducing F-1600-1s exact over-count *inside the check written to cure it*. 📊 **MEASURED, one corpus, three needles, 63 player-path (`src`/`assets`) first-parent commits since 2026-08-05: gazette-only 9-char → 14 absent · whole-outbox 9-char → 10 absent · whole-outbox 8-char → ZERO.** ✓ **I did not trust the zero — I read the matched line for all 10:** `e7bb88cf0` sits in `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md:1349` as `e7bb88cf` (the pick clock), and the other nine in backticked hash runs in the 08-05/08-06 ticker digests (Blackout Ridge, Moth Season, Canyon Works, the Crawler, the E2 socket). Real citations, not prefix collisions. ⚠️ **THIS COSTS MORE THAN THE BLINDNESS IT RESEMBLES:** F-1600-1s failure mode wasted greps and re-judgement; **this one