🔬 **F-1623-1 (s1623 2026-08-10, MEASURED AT THE f1621-1 DRAIN AS ITS OWN CONTROL — THE TOWN-TRANSFER INSTRUMENT CANNOT CURRENTLY ANSWER WHETHER THE BUNDLE IS OVER OR UNDER 25 MB, BECAUSE ITS NOISE FLOOR IS LARGER THAN ITS HEADROOM. THIS SUPERSEDES F-1620-7 AS THE OPEN QUESTION ON THIS THREAD.)** ⚙️ s1621 flagged f1621-1s mobile `normal` arm at **26,542,805** against the 25,000,000 ceiling (headroom **-1,542,805**, assertion RED) and named three candidates to eliminate in order: (1) the new four-cell parameterisation changed what the asserting arms measure; (2) run-to-run instability; (3) a real regression from a merge in the intervening hour. ✅ **The drain ran the identical code ~40 minutes later on the same machine and the suite passed 6/6 on BOTH projects — the red does NOT reproduce.** 📊 **Run 1 (runner 09:18) vs run 2 (drain 09:42), same code, same machine:** A/B `normal` mobile **26,542,805 -> 22,469,496** · desktop **24,604,025 -> 21,297,362** · A/B `saveData` desktop **23,363,925 -> 13,600,227** · cue window **22,497,140 both -> 12,376,473 dsk / 13,942,714 mob** · decomposition `false/false` **19,954,153 / 20,650,367 -> 6,471,185 both, a 3.08x-3.19x swing.** ➡️ **VERDICT ON THE THREE CANDIDATES: (3) REFUTED** (no `src/**` in the diff, asset content-hashes identical across all arms, number came back green unchanged) · **(2) CONFIRMED and dominant** · **(1) CONFIRMED as a real change but NOT the cause** — the runner did replace GLB throttling with a CDP `Network.emulateNetworkConditionsByRule` rule in both tests contrary to the masters explicit "the arms that carry assertions must not change configuration", yet run 2 uses that same new mechanism and is green (**F-1623-2**, non-blocking, recorded). 🎯 **THE LOAD-BEARING CONSEQUENCE: `expect(normalBytes).toBeLessThan(TOWN_TRANSFER_CEILING_BYTES)` is presently a COIN-FLIP** — red for the runner, green for the drain — and it therefore carries no information about the bundle. It is *inherited* from f1619-2 `79782c6b4