🟢 **F-1616-1 (s1616 2026-08-10, MEASURED AT THE f1614-1 DRAIN — A GATE CONDITION WAS SATISFIED IN FORM WHILE CARRYING NO INFORMATION, AND IT WAS UNSATISFIABLE BY CONSTRUCTION, SO NO RUNNER COULD EVER HAVE MET IT AS INTENDED.)** 🧭 **THE CLAUSE.** f1614-1’s master and its BACKLOG gate both demanded *"the prefetch-disabled control showing the WARM column collapse — a table whose warm column is unchanged with the stream off is measuring nothing."* The prescribed control is `/?tier=lite`. The runner ran it, reported `WARM 0/0/0/0/0` on both projects — exactly the column item (e) asked for — and that reads as a pass. ⚠️ **RE-RUN DRAIN-SIDE RATHER THAN INHERITED (Mistake #4), THE CONTROL TABLE IS ALL ZEROS IN *BOTH* COLUMNS**, every door, both projects: `menu 0|0 · town 0|0 · contract1 0|0 · town-return 0|0 · contract2 0|0`. The WARM column does collapse, so the gate is **literally met** — and an all-zero control **cannot distinguish "prefetch stopped warming" from "nothing was requested at all"**, which is precisely the failure the clause was written to prevent, arriving through the one door the clause did not cover. ✓ **VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE BY CONSTRUCTION, WHICH EXONERATES THE RUNNER COMPLETELY:** `src/assets/AdvanceStream.ts:250-252` — `threeDimensionalAssetsEnabled()` — returns false on `terrain2d` **or** `tier=lite`, and that single predicate gates the **whole** 3D asset path, demand-loads included. **There is no prefetch-only disable flag**, so *any* implementation of that control produces an all-zero table. The master asked for one column; the missing column is the one that voids the result. ⭐ **THE DISCRIMINATOR IS NONETHELESS PROVED — BY BETTER EVIDENCE THAT WAS INSIDE THE MAIN ARM ALL ALONG: WITHIN A SINGLE RUN, town reads `2 WARM / 8 COLD` while contract1 reads `7 WARM / 8 COLD`.** A degenerate classifier cannot produce different ratios at different doors of the same run, and that variance reproduced across two independent runs and two projects. **A within-arm comparison beat the prescribed between-arm control, and cost nothing extra.** ➡️ **A REAL CONTROL IS CONSTRUCTIBLE SPEC-SIDE WITH NO `src/` CHANGE:** the spec already installs `page.route('**/*.glb')`, so failing only the requests carrying `x-gold-rush-prefetch: 1` isolates prefetch while leaving the 3D path alive — then assert **COLD > 0** while WARM collapses. That missing `COLD > 0` assertion is the whole defect: it is what let an all-zero table read as a pass. 💡 *Reusable shape: **a control that disables TWO things measures neither.** Before trusting an off-arm, check that the quantity you are NOT testing survived it — an all-zero denominator makes any ratio look like whatever you hoped.* ✅ **CURE AUTHORED THIS FIRE as `f1616-1` (lane-c), folded with F-1616-2.** **GATE: none owed to the owner — spec-side work with a ruling already behind it.**
