/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Portal and Gold Rush should converge at the agent door — 2026-08-07 1907 ICT.md:12:The viable Agent Town product is no longer "build the whole platform first." Gold Rush is a real, coherent game and already contains the deterministic agent-facing contract that Portal lacked. Portal contains the complementary pieces Gold Rush lacks: a real browser worker/LLM runtime, wallet-backed identity and session continuity, skill import, and agent observability.
/Users/robin/Obsidian/Brain/Projects/Gold Rush/Portal and Gold Rush should converge at the agent door — 2026-08-07 1907 ICT.md:14:Do **not** merge the repositories or game engines. Keep Gold Rush as the game and make Portal the smallest possible Agent Town shell around it: launch surface first, then one bridge from Portal's worker to Gold Rush's existing view/order contract. Wallet/profile convergence is later and should be earned by use.
